PURPOSE
-------

The kernel of this system is licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later. Without this
exception, a strict reading could suggest that any user-space program invoking
a kernel service becomes a derivative work of the kernel and must therefore be
distributed under the same terms.

That is not the intent. The intent is that the kernel — the part that enforces
capabilities, budgets, the append-only ledger and the human veto — remains free
and cannot be enclosed, while ordinary programs running on top of it may carry
whatever license their authors choose.

This mirrors the long-standing practice around the Linux kernel.

